Z||000000||Voyd||11-02-1999||04:11 PM||||i just bought an '85 SE and i was wondering, what exactly is the stock sound system in those cars? i think some previous owners changed the stock sound system in my car. there are 2 speakers on the side of the doors, and are of the brand "Alpine".<BR> the there is the speakers in the headrests, and a cheap cassette only radio. <P>thanks for any info. ||||reg||5
Z||000001||DJRice||11-02-1999||04:20 PM||||You should have two 4x10s in the dash, and in that year you will have a pair of small ones in each seat.  As for the radio, there were several versions of a Delco AM/FM that may or may not have a casette player.<P>If the Alpine's are in the door, they were definitely added by previous owner.||||reg||1
Z||000002||RZURCTN||11-03-1999||09:06 PM||||I agree with DJ!  Being an SE it should at least have and AC/Delco AM/FM Stereo Cassette.  If you have something different and want an original, check around the salvage yards.  You can find them in different styles.  Some have a 5 band equalizer while others have simple treble and bass adjustments.  You can even get rebuild kits for them!||||reg||1
Z||000003||Linx||11-04-1999||06:23 PM||||Man- too bad someone perforated his interior door trim with those speakers.   <IMG SRC="http://www.fiero.nl/forum/smile.gif">||||reg||1
